COMPILATION OF: E46N2

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46N2

   1 a 0000 E46N2:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2c] FILE SKIP THEN ONE LITERAL.  CREATE:44 is
   4 a 0006      this shape with 'EOF'; here with 'A' so the pool cell
   5 a 0006      is one byte.  The question is ORDER: does DR attach
   6 a 0006      the SKIP before the item chain (CREATE says yes) and
   7 a 0006      is there one close for the whole statement? */
   8 c 0006   dcl outf file;
   9 c 0006   open file(outf) stream output title('N2OUT DAT');
  10 c 0023   put file(outf) skip list('A');
  11 c 0042   close file(outf);
  12 a 0048 end E46N2;

CODE SIZE = 004B
DATA AREA = 000A
FREE SYMS = 389D
END  COMPILATION
